{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1523156-how-do-you-spot-an-ancient-vampire","id":1523156,"title":"How do you spot an Ancient-Vampire?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-09-25T19:27:30-07:00","id":1523156,"title":"How do you spot an Ancient-Vampire?","content":"They're shorter than your modern-person. They didn't have a modern-diet like we do today. It also would make a difference if the vampire came from an agricultural-society, or a pastoral-society as nomads/herders tend to have a more varied-diet. But, usually, the most exceptional of the society would be made into a vampire, so, expect a height of around 5' 6&quot; to be considered, &quot;Tall&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> They might look, unusual; that is, the human-race slowly changes with time and they might have a facial-feature, that was attractive back then, but as fallen out of favor in modern-times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-26T07:10:30-07:00","id":1523172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1523156-how-do-you-spot-an-ancient-vampire#post1523156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're shorter than your modern-person. They didn't have a modern-diet like we do today. It also would make a difference if the vampire came from an agricultural-society, or a pastoral-society as nomads/herders tend to have a more varied-diet. But, usually, the most exceptional of the society would be made into a vampire, so, expect a height of around 5' 6&quot; to be considered, &quot;Tall&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> They might look, unusual; that is, the human-race slowly changes with time and they might have a facial-feature, that was attractive back then, but as fallen out of favor in modern-times.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Body language (reflective of low humanity, though that does not exactly map to kindred age, far from it), maybe some peculiar accent in the case of those freshly out of torpor (or less caring of adaptability to mortal society as reflected by low humanity).<br /> <br /> The height angle might be helpful - or it might not, depending on social status and acess to a variety of foods in life among other things, plus individuals outside the average. Ramesses IIstands at about 1.7 metres (5 ft 7 in) <i>as a </i><i>mummy</i>\u200b, meaning that he had been taller in life, <i>considerably</i> taller depending on period at times, since the pharaoh was apparently in 90s at the time of his death and people are known to lose a few inches as they age. So 6'+ foot tall royals or aristocrats might be possible even amid the kindred coming from the bronze age.<br /> <br /> And that if you <b>don't</b> account for &quot;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ship_of_Theseus\" target=\"_blank\">ship of theseus</a>/you are what you eat&quot; issues on kindred physical fluidity x body image/self-perception. What can a vampire miss between sleep and hunger frenzy about itself if not constantly, obssessively checking oneself? Would a vampire notice an extra inch per generation or their teeth are whiter than a century before, if that has been the norm for half a century?<br /> <br /> The undead might be <b>not</b> be as unchanging/stagnant in form as they assume themselves to be, if the flesh incrementally adjusts and adapts to better fit unnoticed amidst newer, fresher herds of prey they learn to feed from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-26-2023, 10:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-26T07:45:40-07:00","id":1523175,"title":"","content":"It is easier to eliminate someone as &quot;not ancient&quot; than guaranteeing that someone is.<br /> <br /> Top of my head:<ul><li><b>Ethnic group</b>. Depending on how ancient belonging to certain ethnic groups can discard people.</li> <li><b>Language</b>. Clearly if the vampire does not speak anything that has a recently equivalent they are either old or from an isolated region.</li> <li><b>Tooth health</b>. Tooth hygiene is relatively recent and was one of the things that people did not take care of, their regular human teeth (not their fangs) <i>could </i>be an indicator.</li> <li><b>Age of embrace</b>. People did not tend to live to old age in ancient times, so an old presenting vampire is unlikely to be ancient (except perhaps as part of their curse or bloodline characteristics).</li> <li><b>Scars and missing limbs</b>. Ancient times were brutal and not only in conflict, the lack of medical knowledge meant that things are minor inconveniences today could have been lethal or life impairing then.</li> <li><b>Height</b>. Changes in diet and nutritional content, show that we have progressively grown taller, but there are always outliers AND if the person was prosperous in their time they might have been taller than their contemporaries.</li> <li><b>Social expectations</b>. Opinion on other ethnic groups, slavery, women rights, children duties, etc, can all be reflective not of a conservative mindset but of a truly OLD society.</li> </ul>So with all of those, you have a reasonable, but by no means certain, way of eliminating factors based on that you have a better than guessing chance of finding an ancient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":".  Fixed content. 09-26-2023, 10:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-26T07:57:44-07:00","id":1523176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1523156-how-do-you-spot-an-ancient-vampire?p=1523175#post1523175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is easier to eliminate someone as &quot;not ancient&quot; than guaranteeing that someone is.<br /> <br /> Top of my head:<ul><li><b>Ethnic group</b>. Depending on how ancient belonging to certain ethnic groups can discard people.</li> <li><b>Language</b>. Clearly if the vampire does not speak anything that has a recently equivalent they are either old or from an isolated region.</li> <li><b>Tooth health</b>. Tooth hygiene is relatively recent and was one of the things that people did not take care of, their regular human teeth (not their fangs) <i>could </i>be an indicator.</li> <li><b>Age of embrace</b>. People did not tend to live to old age in ancient times, so an old presenting vampire is unlikely to be ancient (except perhaps as part of their curse or bloodline characteristics).</li> <li><b>Scars and missing limbs</b>. Ancient times were brutal and not only in conflict, the lack of medical knowledge meant that things are minor inconveniences today could have been lethal or life impairing then.</li> <li><b>Height</b>. Changes in diet and nutritional content, show that we have progressively grown taller, but there are always outliers AND if the person was prosperous in their time they might have been taller than their contemporaries.</li> <li><b>Social expectations</b>. Opinion on other ethnic groups, slavery, women rights, children duties, etc, can all be reflective not of a conservative mindset but of a truly OLD society.</li> </ul>So with all of those, you have a reasonable, but by no means certain, way of eliminating factors based on that you have a better than guessing chance of finding an ancient.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So based on that, someone that only speaks Sanskrit (or Latin or an unrecognized language), is between 160 and 170cm tall, is missing teeth, looks like a teen or young adult COULD be ancient.<br /> <br /> They could also be someone from a unprivileged background pretending to be ancient and trying to intimidate people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 09-26-2023, 11:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-26T11:10:05-07:00","id":1523181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1523156-how-do-you-spot-an-ancient-vampire#post1523156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're shorter than your modern-person. They didn't have a modern-diet like we do today. It also would make a difference if the vampire came from an agricultural-society, or a pastoral-society as nomads/herders tend to have a more varied-diet. But, usually, the most exceptional of the society would be made into a vampire, so, expect a height of around 5' 6&quot; to be considered, &quot;Tall&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> They might look, unusual; that is, the human-race slowly changes with time and they might have a facial-feature, that was attractive back then, but as fallen out of favor in modern-times.</div> </div> </div> </div>A mild counter to this that's <i>mostly </i>going to be relevant for ancient Gangrel and Gangrel-predecessors: Protean has a fair number of Devotions that allow a vampire to permanently change their physical appearance. Devotions rooted in Nightmare and Majesty also often have similar (if not as extensive) effects\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1523156-how-do-you-spot-an-ancient-vampire?p=1523175#post1523175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is easier to eliminate someone as &quot;not ancient&quot; than guaranteeing that someone is.<br /> <br /> Top of my head:<ul><li><b>Ethnic group</b>. Depending on how ancient belonging to certain ethnic groups can discard people.</li> <li><b>Language</b>. Clearly if the vampire does not speak anything that has a recently equivalent they are either old or from an isolated region.</li> <li><b>Tooth health</b>. Tooth hygiene is relatively recent and was one of the things that people did not take care of, their regular human teeth (not their fangs) <i>could </i>be an indicator.</li> <li><b>Age of embrace</b>. People did not tend to live to old age in ancient times, so an old presenting vampire is unlikely to be ancient (except perhaps as part of their curse or bloodline characteristics).</li> <li><b>Scars and missing limbs</b>. Ancient times were brutal and not only in conflict, the lack of medical knowledge meant that things are minor inconveniences today could have been lethal or life impairing then.</li> <li><b>Height</b>. Changes in diet and nutritional content, show that we have progressively grown taller, but there are always outliers AND if the person was prosperous in their time they might have been taller than their contemporaries.</li> <li><b>Social expectations</b>. Opinion on other ethnic groups, slavery, women rights, children duties, etc, can all be reflective not of a conservative mindset but of a truly OLD society.</li> </ul>So with all of those, you have a reasonable, but by no means certain, way of eliminating factors based on that you have a better than guessing chance of finding an ancient.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some counter points:<br /> <br /> <b>Language</b>: The big thing of the matter on this one is that unless you're talking about people suffering truly huge leaps due to torpor, most leaps are going to to be within the reach of a century*, so most of the time the language leap isn't going to be that much. THis is also compounded by the problem that vampires, though not subject to the Fog of Ages as in First Edition, can forget things, and as languages die and there's less need to practice them, it's unlikely that you're ancient vampires are going to be using things like the spoken form of Linear B.<br /> <b>Tooth Health</b><b>:</b> We have proof that as far back as the Neolithic Age (and we're talking early Neolithic, about 13,000 years ago) that civilizations were in the business of doing forms of dental cleaning (albeit in the form of scrapping plaque from teeth with primitive tools), and as far back as 2660 BCE we start seeing the development of mouth washes, specific locals for the gums, and application of antiseptics in Egypt, and on the Indian Pennisula, the practice of brushing teeth with paste and a soft piece of shrub was encouraged by the Vedic texts and proved pretty damn effective, and even practiced a form of braces to support looser teeth. Greece wouldn't be too far behind on these ideas, since Aristotle(philosopher) and Hippocrates(medical scholar) both mention similar practices in their own texts. The Olmec people regularly made pastes for the purposes of cleaning teeth that are proven to be effective to this day. There's lots of evidence for pretty sophisticated dental practices for the time, and while modern dentistry is definitely a lot more advanced than it was in old time, oral hygiene and tooth structure from ancient peoples likely isn't particularly any worse than people of low income today, particularly for any vampires who come from the upper classes of their home place and time.<br /> <b>Age of Embrace</b><b>:</b> Again, sort of depends on the region and time period you're talking about, and also how you define old age. While the modern world is setting records for the average regular old age, certain periods of time had systems of medical support and good circumstances that could regularly get people going to their 60s. Contrawise, there's also the vampiric predilection against Embracing anyone too young or too old because guess what you have to deal with for eternity, which is going to be the larger contributor towards certain ranges of adolescence in vampiric communities.<br /> <b>Scars and Missing Limbs: </b>Ironically, what you point out is more likely to contribute to them <i>not</i> missing limbs, because too much of a limb loss more likely just led straight to death. The brutality of the times is also not a given? A lot of places in time were pretty decent for living in, again at particular different classes, but even peasantry (and depending again on the time period and location, even the enslaved) very often didn't face brutality in the way you're implying.<br /> <b>Societal Expectations:</b> You're actually dead on about this, but for the benefits of people who might not know better, ancient societies didn't have racism, sexism, or a lot of the other isms in the way we experience it modernly(and some societies at times didn't even have some of the ones you'd think they have, like racism), and a lifetime through the lens of vampirism very likely sands down bigotry, for practical purposes if nothing else. I'm not saying ancient vampries are secretly social justice corpses, in advance, just that a lot of the ideas that social justice issues are centered on aren't universal and ancient features of human society and pragmatism has a way of discarding certain biases. <hr />Part of the reason why truly ancient vampires are troublesome on a scale that puts them on par with Strix is that, for all that you might think there'd be certain tells for them, they actually likely to blend in more than not. It's nice to think you could spot the Methuselah Zagreus out of a lineup of Mehket**, but honestly you've got about the same chance as spotting someone ridden by an Owl, and by the time you realize you got the wrong guy, your average Methuselash probably has the domain playing to their tune, if that's what they're interested in.<br /> <br /> *To really get long torpor sessions requires both low Humanity and high Blood Potency to really get going, where as the stereotypical average for an elder suffering from their hubris or misfortune, usually depicted around Humanity 4-3, Blood Potency 7-8, is regularly going to suffer within the reach of 7 years to 40 years of downtime. Vampires can definitely hit those higher points with Humanity 2-1 and Blood Potency 9-10, but those are statistically likely to be outliers even in conversations about truly ancient vampires, and I'd personally wager most truly ancient vampires who had those sort of massive torpors likely had them long before getting to the modern era-mistakes like that are more the realm of what truly ancient vampires would likely call &quot;youth&quot;, even if no one else would.<br /> **Figuratively speaking, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-26T14:35:53-07:00","id":1523186,"title":"","content":"Ultimately, I think the biggest problem is that any vampire that survives as a vampire long enough to qualify as a Methuselah is going to have to have developed social adaptability skills. Given how rapidly human cultures in a given area can change in a few decades, let along centuries, the longer an undeath, the more vampire needs to develop methods of keeping up with the times (relying on younger vampires to do all that for them is a great way to get screwed by them instead). A vampire Embrace when Rome was still a Republic, and that tries to keep acting according to the mannerism, language, and cultural norm of the day wouldn't have been likely to survive the Roman imperial period without other vampires deciding it was too revealing to the humans and doing something about it. While there's always room to play things off as liking old-fashioned stuff, being a foreigner, and so on the help smooth over minor thing, if you can't adapt socially, you aren't making it that long as a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-26T15:04:14-07:00","id":1523188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1523156-how-do-you-spot-an-ancient-vampire?p=1523172#post1523172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Body language (reflective of low humanity, though that does not exactly map to kindred age, far from it), maybe some peculiar accent in the case of those freshly out of torpor (or less caring of adaptability to mortal society as reflected by low humanity).<br /> <br /> The height angle might be helpful - or it might not, depending on social status and acess to a variety of foods in life among other things, plus individuals outside the average. Ramesses IIstands at about 1.7 metres (5 ft 7 in) <i>as a </i><i>mummy</i>\u200b, meaning that he had been taller in life, <i>considerably</i> taller depending on period at times, since the pharaoh was apparently in 90s at the time of his death and people are known to lose a few inches as they age. So 6'+ foot tall royals or aristocrats might be possible even amid the kindred coming from the bronze age.<br /> <br /> And that if you <b>don't</b> account for &quot;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ship_of_Theseus\" target=\"_blank\">ship of theseus</a>/you are what you eat&quot; issues on kindred physical fluidity x body image/self-perception. What can a vampire miss between sleep and hunger frenzy about itself if not constantly, obssessively checking oneself? Would a vampire notice an extra inch per generation or their teeth are whiter than a century before, if that has been the norm for half a century?<br /> <br /> The undead might be <b>not</b> be as unchanging/stagnant in form as they assume themselves to be, if the flesh incrementally adjusts and adapts to better fit unnoticed amidst newer, fresher herds of prey they learn to feed from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ramesy did have a very good diet, being the son of a pharaoh and yes, he was probably over six-feet when he was in his early-20's. <br /> <br /> As for the Ship of Theseus, while, most vampires are considered, &quot;Unaging&quot;, and, &quot;Unchanging&quot;, most vampires, are lucky if they make it to the century-mark. When half the world is hostile to you and can give you a really, really, bad sun-burn, and living in a society of other vampires, all which are out for blood (literally), doesn't make the odds of a long-life good. Ricean vampires become more stone-like as they aged. But, since Blood-Potency, the hallmark of age, of sorts, can decrease, I tend to think of Requiem-Vampires as, well, stuck in their old bodies, never changing. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1523156-how-do-you-spot-an-ancient-vampire?p=1523175#post1523175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is easier to eliminate someone as &quot;not ancient&quot; than guaranteeing that someone is.<br /> <br /> Top of my head:<ul><li><b>Ethnic group</b>. Depending on how ancient belonging to certain ethnic groups can discard people.</li> <li><b>Language</b>. Clearly if the vampire does not speak anything that has a recently equivalent they are either old or from an isolated region.</li> <li><b>Tooth health</b>. Tooth hygiene is relatively recent and was one of the things that people did not take care of, their regular human teeth (not their fangs) <i>could </i>be an indicator.</li> <li><b>Age of embrace</b>. People did not tend to live to old age in ancient times, so an old presenting vampire is unlikely to be ancient (except perhaps as part of their curse or bloodline characteristics).</li> <li><b>Scars and missing limbs</b>. Ancient times were brutal and not only in conflict, the lack of medical knowledge meant that things are minor inconveniences today could have been lethal or life impairing then.</li> <li><b>Height</b>. Changes in diet and nutritional content, show that we have progressively grown taller, but there are always outliers AND if the person was prosperous in their time they might have been taller than their contemporaries.</li> <li><b>Social expectations</b>. Opinion on other ethnic groups, slavery, women rights, children duties, etc, can all be reflective not of a conservative mindset but of a truly OLD society.</li> </ul>So with all of those, you have a reasonable, but by no means certain, way of eliminating factors based on that you have a better than guessing chance of finding an ancient.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ethnic groups do tend to change, but sometimes, not as much; most Italians look the same way they did during pre-Roman times, including the Etruscans. <br /> <br /> Language is important, and how they speak; an ancient vampire from Shakespeare's London wouldn't sound like a normal Londoner with their British accent; they'd talk like a pirate (Aye, an' ye bar-wench bent over, out came a gust of wind). <br /> <br /> Tooth decay is a good indication; but, depends on class and age of embrace; and in some cases, lifestyle; pastoralists didn't eat a lot of wheat-products, and their teeth didn't decay as fast and horticulturalists did. <br /> <br /> And speaking of Age of Embrace, the Medieval-times, was, in fact, full of young children given the high birth-rates and high child-mortality. So chances are, any vampire that remembers Edward II, will most likely be a teenager. <br /> <br /> I'd say, the lack of good medical-knowledge means that most people, didn't survive to have a scar. <br /> <br /> A vampire will have some anachronisms, if they remember; the mind is finite and doesn't remember all. Surely an ancient-vampire can have a Aristotelian-view that some people require masters etc. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-26T17:16:50-07:00","id":1523192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1523156-how-do-you-spot-an-ancient-vampire?p=1523175#post1523175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is easier to eliminate someone as &quot;not ancient&quot; than guaranteeing that someone is.<br /> <br /> Top of my head:<ul><li><b>Ethnic group</b>. Depending on how ancient belonging to certain ethnic groups can discard people.<br /> <br /> I can agree with this statement. But at some point an ancient would become very pragmatic and would work with people that his or her tribe used to detest to further there own interests.</li> <li><b>Language</b>. Clearly if the vampire does not speak anything that has a recently equivalent they are either old or from an isolated region.<br /> <br /> Or the vampire in question knows and is fluent in numerous dead dialects or speaks at times using ancient terms for things they struggle with as they grasp with changes in languages as certain words or phrases meanings have changed or no longer used .</li> <li><b>Tooth health</b>. Tooth hygiene is relatively recent and was one of the things that people did not take care of, their regular human teeth (not their fangs) <i>could </i>be an indicator.<br /> <br /> That may not be a good indictor for spotting an ancient vampire. It's quite possible that the Beast would fix the teeth over time for more effective hunting of their prey. So I would leave this one off the table so to speak.</li> <li><b>Age of embrace</b>. People did not tend to live to old age in ancient times, so an old presenting vampire is unlikely to be ancient (except perhaps as part of their curse or bloodline</li> <li>True it wouldn't be shocking that some the eldest vampires would look to be in there mid to late teens with being in there early twenties on the extreme end.</li> <li>characteristics).</li> <li><b>Scars and missing limbs</b>. Ancient times were brutal and not only in conflict, the lack of medical knowledge meant that things are minor inconveniences today could have been lethal or life impairing then.<br /> <br /> Not always a good pointer for age, even elders from a few centuries ago would suffer from lack of medical knowledge or how using proper hygiene would lower the risks of disease.</li> <li><b>Height</b>. Changes in diet and nutritional content, show that we have progressively grown taller, but there are always outliers AND if the person was prosperous in their time they might have been taller than their contemporaries.<br /> <br /> Indeed that would be quite possible as wealthier families would be taller then average.</li> <li><b>Social expectations</b>. Opinion on other ethnic groups, slavery, women rights, children duties, etc, can all be reflective not of a conservative mindset but of a truly OLD society.</li> </ul>So with all of those, you have a reasonable, but by no means certain, way of eliminating factors based on that you have a better than guessing chance of finding an ancient.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or a very detached mindset as they would find things like skin color, gender, idealogies and or sexual orientation very meaningless as they have seen civilizations rise and fall way to many times and see the latest trends as fads that will pass very quickly in their eyes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-27-2023, 02:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T14:01:52-07:00","id":1523234,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's raised explicitly, but reading between the lines, I think torpor would probably deal with the language problem in most cases, possibly the same for social attitudes.<br /> <br /> Like, we know that post-torpor kindred are essentially tuned to update themselves to their present surroundings, so I could see language and social norms being part of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T18:59:51-07:00","id":1523247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1523156-how-do-you-spot-an-ancient-vampire?p=1523234#post1523234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it's raised explicitly, but reading between the lines, I think torpor would probably deal with the language problem in most cases, possibly the same for social attitudes.<br /> <br /> Like, we know that post-torpor kindred are essentially tuned to update themselves to their present surroundings, so I could see language and social norms being part of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, from the corebook:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p67</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Our dead minds are active during torpor. They hone themselves on nightmares, preparing for the ever more modern world. This Long Night of the Soul purifies us for our ghastly purpose. <b>The elders awaken with soft, pliable minds. They mimic the herd, picking up new tricks with the frightening alacrity of a toddler playing with a smartphone.</b> An elder who went to sleep after the Great Chicago Fire recently showed me how to use this thing called Twitter.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p105</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When one of the Kindred falls to torpor, she appears dead. Her skin tightens over her flesh and dries out. Her joints harden, and the top layer of her tissue turns to a faint, ashen dust. <b>During her slumber, she experiences strange, nonsensical dreams that keep her mind active and exercised. Usually, this\u200b means she\u2019s prepared to adapt to a new world.</b> Sometimes, this goes awry; she wakes up a whole new person, or, rarely, with distorted memories of her past existence.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p107-108</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Breaking points don\u2019t occur while a character is in torpor. At the Storyteller\u2019s discretion, discovering a missed breaking point <u>could</u> trigger a detachment roll, but this is fairly rare, as <b>the experience of torpor prepares a vampire\u2019s mind for the shock of a new world upon waking.</b>\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}